### animeko  (AGPLv3)

This repository contains source code derived from the animeko project by
OpenAni and contributors:

    https://github.com/open-ani/animeko

The ported code is the video player UI layer: gesture handling, controller
visibility arbitration, progress sliders and drag preview, the player
scaffold, top bar, playback-speed and aspect-ratio controls, and supporting
utilities. It lives mainly in the `:video:ui` module
(`video/ui/src/*Main/kotlin/lovehan1me/video/player/ui/`), plus a small number
of contract types in `:video:contract` and the player screen layout in
`:shared`. Each derived file carries a header naming animeko as its source and
pointing at the AGPLv3 terms; those headers must be preserved when the code is
redistributed.

Two bundled GLSL shader assets used by the Android super-resolution scaling
pass are also copied from animeko's shader resources:

    video/engine/src/commonMain/composeResources/files/shaders/exo-effects/ewa_lanczossharp.vert
    video/engine/src/commonMain/composeResources/files/shaders/exo-effects/ewa_lanczossharp.frag

They are distributed under the GNU AGPLv3 as part of this work. These two files
are kept byte-for-byte as upstream wrote them (a leading comment before
`#version` is rejected by some Android GL drivers, and the whole point of the
scaling pass is that it compiles everywhere), so their attribution lives here
instead of in a header comment.

Because these components are AGPLv3, the combined work in this repository is
offered under AGPLv3 (see the note at the top of this file).


